Version: 1.0
desc: Brick by Brick Convolution Reverb (x42 Convolver port) by chmaha
tags: reverb convolution impulse response hall room chamber plate
author: chmaha
changelog:
  Initial release.
about:
  Convolution reverb with 134 hall, room, chamber, plate, space and ambience programs, each in a true-stereo
  version and a mono-to-stereo version. The convolution engine splits the impulse response into partitions that
  grow with distance from the start, so long halls stay light on the CPU; Zero Latency switches to a direct-form head for no delay at all.
  Ported from the x42 Convolver (zeroconvo.lv2) by Robin Gareus
  https://github.com/x42/zconvo.lv2 (GPL-3.0-or-later, convolution engine by Fons Adriaensen)
  Impulse responses: Samplicity's Bricasti M7 impulse response library, free for non-commercial use
  (see Dependencies/BrickByBrick/BrickByBrick-LICENSE.txt), with the level matching from the x42 presets
  JSFX version released under GPL-3.0-or-later
  Claude generated some of this code
